ode where possible.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["Building Footprints","Building Outlines","Structure","Location","SGID","UGRC"],"snippet":"Building footprints of Utah","thumbnail":"thumbnail/location.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-114.0491008288653,36.997932755186206],[-109.04167266037712,42.00062625451114]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"Microsoft, OpenStreetMap contributors, and UGRC","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<p style='margin:0;'><span>This data is derived from Microsoft Building Footprints and OpenStreetMap and carries the same license.<\/span><\/p><p style='margin:0;'>&nbsp;<\/p><p style='margin:0;'><span>OpenStreetMap® is <\/span><i><span>open data<\/span><\/i><span>, licensed under the <\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span>Open Data Commons Open Database License<\/span><\/a><span>(ODbL) by the <\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://osmfoundation.org' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span>OpenStreetMap Foundation<\/span><\/a><span>(OSMF).<\/span><\/p><p style='margin:0;'><span>You are free to copy, distribute, transmit and adapt our data, as long as you credit OpenStreetMap and its contributors. If you alter or build upon our data, you may distribute the result only under the same license. The full <\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span>legal code<\/span><\/a><span>, explains your rights and responsibilities.<\/span><\/p><p style='margin:0;'>&nbsp;<\/p><p style='margin:0;'><span>© OpenStreetMap contributors<\/span><\/p><p style='margin:0;'><span>For more information, visit <\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span>https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright<\/span><\/a><span>, <\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://www.openstreetmap.org' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span>https://www.openstreetmap.org<\/span><\/a><span>, and <\/span><a target='_blank' href='https://opendatacommons.org' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span>https://opendatacommons.org<\/span><\/a><span>.<\/span><\/p>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/99lidPhWCzftIe9K/arcgis/rest/services/Buildings/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":46695,"contentStatus":"public_authoritative","orgId":"99lidPhWCzftIe9K","scoreCompleteness":90,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791910800000,"source":"Utah Automated Geographic Reference Center (AGRC)"},{"id":"a226b9f824124e09a4d697480aa0f391","owner":"Garrett_utco","created":1670262178000,"modified":1778771853000,"guid":null,"name":"2022_General_Voter_Location_Analysis_WFL1","title":"2022 General Voter Location Analysis_WFL1","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Multilayer","Service","Hosted Service"],"description":"<p><strong>Overview<\/strong><\/p><p>This feature service presents a comprehensive geographic and tabular dataset focused on voter locations, precinct boundaries, voting centers, early and election day voters, and building outlines within Utah County. It integrates detailed spatial and attribute information supporting election planning, voter analysis, and civic infrastructure monitoring in the county.<\/p><p><strong>Feature Layers<\/strong><\/p><ul><li><strong>Election Voting Centers and Dropboxes<\/strong>: This layer identifies locations of voting centers and ballot dropboxes, including attributes like type, location, address, active status, and links to images and maps, facilitating public awareness and accessibility of voting facilities.<\/li><li><strong>Voting Precincts (Early and Election Day)<\/strong>: Updated precinct boundary layers capture the detailed geographic extents of early voting and election day precincts. These include political district alignments (congressional, state senate, house, local boards), and distribution of voting locations, supporting electoral districting and resource allocation.<\/li><li><strong>Building Outlines<\/strong>: Detailed footprints of ground floor structures across Utah County are represented with associated facility types such as government, educational, religious, commercial, and residential buildings. This dataset supports local government planning, public safety, and land use management related to voter infrastructure and community services.<\/li><li><strong>Early Voters and Voter Addresses<\/strong>: Multiple layers and tables capture the spatial locations and attribute details of early voters, including party affiliation, addresses, precincts, and voting counts. Hotspot analysis data highlights spatial patterns in voter distributions. These datasets are crucial for analyzing voter behavior and turnout patterns in early voting campaigns.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Geographic Coverage<\/strong><\/p><p>The service covers Utah County in the state of Utah, USA, including cities within the county such as American Fork, Lehi, Orem, Provo, Spanish Fork, and others. It supports county-wide election planning and demographic analysis.<\/p><p><strong>Use Cases<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Planning and managing voting locations and dropbox accessibility.<\/li><li>Analyzing voter turnout and early voting trends spatially and temporally.<\/li><li>Supporting election officials in precinct boundary management and electoral district updates.<\/li><li>Local government use for infrastructure planning, public safety, and land use related to electoral facilities.<\/li><\/ul>","tags":["Utah County","voting locations","precinct boundaries","early voting","building footprints","election analysis","voter distribution"],"snippet":"Comprehensive Utah County dataset featuring voting centers, precinct boundaries, building footprints, and early voter spatial analysis for election planning and voter behavior understanding.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-112.22035023626985,39.772456097450494],[-110.85060791360826,40.5816299272633]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102100","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services1.arcgis.com/9DapJHuwsEakbYuW/arcgis/rest/services/2022_General_Voter_Location_Analysis_WFL1/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":2771,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791874800000,"source":"Utah County"},{"id":"bae2efcd33314a8188060be84ba02ba5","owner":"lehicity","created":1738856234000,"modified":1738856243000,"guid":null,"name":"Lehi City - FEMA BRIC Study - Flood Inundation Area - Benefited Structures","title":"Lehi City - FEMA BRIC Study - Flood Inundation Area - Benefited Structures","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Service","Singlelayer","Hosted Service"],"description":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span>This polygon feature layer is derived from the Utah County Data Sharing Hub - Building Footprints dataset (https://utah-county-data-sharing-hub-utahcounty.hub.arcgis.com)<\/span><\/p><p><span>The shape and orientation of the ground floor of all structures in Utah County. This information is typically compiled from orthoimagery or other aerial photography sources. <\/span><\/p><p><span>Additional attribute data were spatially joined to the building layer from the Utah County parcel layer. Additional elevation and depth attribute values were added from modeled raster data, using the 'Add Surface Information' geoprocessing tool.<\/span><\/p><p><span>Published on: 20-June-2024<\/span><\/p><p><span>Data accuracy: Approximate and modeled data<\/span><\/p><p><span>JDE Project number and name: 2012-034 Lehi City FEMA BRIC Funding and Flood Study<\/span><\/p><p><span>Geographic project location: Lehi City, Utah County, Utah, USA<\/span><\/p><p><span>Coordinate system/transformation used: NAD 1983 State Plane Utah Central FIPS 4302 (US Feet)<\/span><\/p><p><span>GIS Software/Version used: ArcGIS Pro 3.3.0<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","tags":["Utah County","buildings","building footprints","building outlines","structures"],"snippet":"Lehi City - FEMA BRIC Study - Flood Inundation Area - Benefited Structures","thumbnail":"thumbnail/Lehi_City___FEMA_BRIC_Study___Flood_Inundation_Area___Benefited_Structures.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-111.90054817107946,40.36294556147505],[-111.84361187423838,40.398483718215786]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"102743","accessInformation":"Building Footprint Origin: GIS Division of the Utah County Information Systems Department\nProject Data Management: Jesse Miller. GIS Specialist\nContact Phone: 435-896-8266 \nContact Email: jesse.m@jonesanddemille.com \nJones & DeMille Engineering \nDate: 20-June-2024","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"<div style='text-align:Left;'><div><div><p><span>Not Restricted<\/span><\/p><p style='margin:0 0 11 0;'><span>These GIS Data are for informational purposes only and should be field verified prior to use in project design.<\/span><\/p><p style='margin:0 0 11 0;'><span>Every effort is made to provide and maintain accurate, complete, and timely data. However, neither Jones &amp; DeMille Engineering or any of its employees make any warranty, expressed or implied, nor assume any legal liability or responsibility for the accuracy, completeness, or usefulness of this data.<\/span><\/p><\/div><\/div><\/div>","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services5.arcgis.com/rObWD7PYeLl9jJPT/arcgis/rest/services/Lehi City - FEMA BRIC Study - Flood Inundation Area - Benefited Structures/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":161,"scoreCompleteness":100,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791878400000,"licenseConstraintId":"custom"},{"id":"d65e8522086b4b6086cf6f11c6c98e3c","owner":"Brady.Cervetti@hdrinc.com_HDR","created":1774368277000,"modified":1781293418000,"guid":null,"name":"Northern_Utah_PEL_Data","title":"Northern Utah Environmental and Infrastructure Data","type":"Feature Service","typeKeywords":["ArcGIS Server","Data","Feature Access","Feature Service","Metadata","Multilayer","Service","Hosted Service"],"description":"<b>Overview<\/b><p>This comprehensive dataset provides extensive geographic information covering various environmental, water resource, community facilities, hazardous waste, air quality, species habitats, trails, parks, and parcel data, primarily focusing on Northern Utah and Utah County. The collection consolidates multiple feature layers to support diverse applications including environmental management, urban planning, natural resource conservation, and public infrastructure developments.<\/p><b>Feature Layers<\/b><ul><li><b>Environmental and Water Resources<\/b>: Includes layers such as NRCS Soil Survey Utah County providing detailed soil characteristics, Assessed Lakes, Utah NWI wetlands inventory, Utah County Floodplains, Utah Assessed Waters, Source Water Assessment Zones, Ground Water and Surface Water Source Protection Zones, Water System Facilities, Water Rights Area, Springs, Waste Water Treatment Plants, Pipelines, Reservoirs, and significant data on hazardous areas like Voluntary Cleanup Program, Toxic Release Inventory, CERCLA lists, Petroleum Storage Tanks, and Military Munitions Response sites.<\/li><li><b>Community Facilities and Public Services<\/b>: Contains data on Fire Stations, Churches, Public Libraries, Historic Buildings, Architectural Surveys, Historic Districts, Licensed Health Care Facilities, Schools (PreK to 12), and Government Buildings, supporting civic and social infrastructure analyses.<\/li><li><b>Air Quality and Environmental Health<\/b>: Includes specific layers covering air quality maintenance areas such as Utah County PM 10 Maintenance Area and Provo PM 2.5 Maintenance Area, along with MS4 Permits to monitor stormwater systems.<\/li><li><b>Biodiversity and Conservation<\/b>: Detailed species habitat layers including Utah Pronghorn Habitat, Utah Mule Deer Habitat, Yellow-billed Cuckoo Current Range, June Sucker, Migration Corridors and Stopover sites, and Wildlife Management Areas (WMA) foster wildlife conservation and habitat protection efforts.<\/li><li><b>Recreation and Trails<\/b>: Features multiple trail systems including UTN Master Plan and UGRC Trails, and park data encompassing Local Parks and Utah State Parks, facilitating recreation planning and natural resource enjoyment.<\/li><li><b>Land Ownership and Parcel Data<\/b>: Comprises comprehensive parcel datasets including all parcels, DNR parcels, parcels owned by the U.S. government, and Utah Sovereign Land, essential for property management, land use planning, and legal assessments.<\/li><\/ul><b>Geographic Coverage<\/b><p>The dataset covers Northern Utah with a focus on Utah County, providing detailed spatial representations relevant for state and county level resource management and urban development.<\/p><b>Applications<\/b><ul><li>Environmental assessment and natural resource conservation<\/li><li>Urban planning and infrastructure development<\/li><li>Water resource management and protection zone delineation<\/li><li>Public safety and community services mapping<\/li><li>Wildlife habitat conservation and migration studies<\/li><li>Recreation and trail management<\/li><li>Land and property ownership analysis<\/li><\/ul><b>Data Integration and Utility<\/b><p>This multi-layered dataset integrates diverse sources of geographic information into a singular resource suitable for GIS professionals, environmental scientists, urban planners, and government officials for informed decision-making and public service management.<\/p>","tags":["Utah County","Northern Utah","Environmental Data","Water Resources","Community Facilities","Wildlife Habitat","Air Quality","Land Parcels","Conservation","Recreation Trails"],"snippet":"Comprehensive Northern Utah dataset encompassing environmental, water, community facilities, air quality, wildlife habitats, trails, parks, and parcel ownership information, focused on Utah County.","thumbnail":"thumbnail/thumbnail.png","documentation":null,"extent":[[-112.86985220962895,-14.624727387140359],[-8.983334375909707E-4,71.08196305439803]],"categories":[],"spatialReference":"103170","accessInformation":"","classification":null,"licenseInfo":"","culture":"en-us","properties":null,"advancedSettings":null,"url":"https://services.arcgis.com/04HiymDgLlsbhaV4/arcgis/rest/services/Northern_Utah_PEL_Data/FeatureServer","proxyFilter":null,"access":"public","size":-1,"subInfo":0,"appCategories":[],"industries":[],"languages":[],"largeThumbnail":null,"banner":null,"screenshots":[],"listed":false,"numComments":0,"numRatings":0,"avgRating":0,"numViews":14062,"scoreCompleteness":83,"groupDesignations":null,"apiToken1ExpirationDate":-1,"apiToken2ExpirationDate":-1,"lastViewed":1791910800000,"source":"HDR ArcGIS Online"},{"id":"9bf5ad81c3314de2892a114cbba9063b","owner":"dkensok_osm","created":1609979176000,"modified