tifying buildings along with address and parcel reference details where available.<\/p><p><strong>Contents<\/strong><\/p><ul><li><strong>Structure footprints<\/strong> representing buildings within the affected wildfire area.<\/li><li><strong>Structure attributes<\/strong> including name, address, city, county, ZIP code, parcel identifier, source year, and damage classification.<\/li><li><strong>Damage status<\/strong> values that describe the observed or reported impact to each structure, including None, Affected, Minimal, Major, and Destroyed.<\/li><\/ul><p><strong>Source Information<\/strong><\/p><p>The structure footprints are derived from building footprint data and enriched with local geographic reference information. The service is organized for operational use in wildfire response and situational awareness.<\/p><p><strong>Geographic Coverage<\/strong><\/p><p>The layer covers the Cottonwood Fire area in Utah and includes structures located within the fire-affected region.<\/p><p><strong>Use Cases<\/strong><\/p><ul><li>Wildfire incident mapping and damage assessment<\/li><li>Structure-level situational awareness for emergency management<\/li><li>Field verification and response planning<\/li><li>Impact review using address, parcel, and county reference information<\/li><\/ul><h3><span style='font-size:18px;'><span><strong>Accessibility<\/strong><\/span><\/span><\/h3><p><span style='font-size:inherit;'><span>For accessibility assistance, contact <strong>Julia Surkis (DEM GIS Program Manager)<\/strong> at <\/span><\/span><a href='mailto:jsurkis@utah.gov' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'><span style='font-size:inherit;'><span>jsurkis@utah.gov<\/span><\/span><\/a><span style='font-size:inherit;'><span>.<\/span><\/span><\/p>","tags":["Cottonwood Fire","wildfire","Utah","buildings","structures","damage assessment","incident response","parcel data","address points"],"snippet":"Building footprints and structure status for the Cottonwood Fire area 